  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shiv Shankar Sahu vs State Of U.P. on 1 April, 2024 Author: Ajit Kumar Bench: Ajit Kumar High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc:54867 Court No. - 4 Case :- Matters Under Article 227 No. - 2444 of 2024 Petitioner :- Shiv Shankar Sahu Respondent :- State of U.P. Counsel for Petitioner :- Abhay Raj Yadav,Neeraj Pandey,Shilpa Singh Sikarwar",
    "facts": "By means of this petition filed under Article 227 of the Constitution, petitioner before this Court wants expeditious disposal of the pending injunction application filed in Food Safety Appeal No.- 51 of 2021 as according to him the opposite party is proceeding with recovery pursuant to the order passed by the Additional District Magistrate (Administration) under Section 52 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 dated 23rd September, 2021.",
    "arguments": "At this stage, learned counsel for the petitioner states that 27th March, 2024 was fixed in the matter but since there was a direction for no adverse order, the matter could not be disposed of. He submits that opposite party is proceeding with recovery.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "At this stage, learned counsel for the petitioner states that 27th March, 2024 was fixed in the matter but since there was a direction for no adverse order, the matter could not be disposed of. He submits that opposite party is proceeding with recovery.",
